## Formal core

Let time be represented by real time (t\in\mathbb{R}*{\ge 0}) and a **legal time-quantum map** (Q*\Delta:\mathbb{R}*{\ge 0}\to \Delta\mathbb{Z}*{\ge 0}) (e.g., “snap to the nearest legal quantum” subject to a rule-set), where (\Delta>0) is the base quantum.

Let the environment be a directed multigraph
[
G=(P,E),\qquad E\subseteq P\times P,
]
where (P) are **places** and (E) are **corridors** (directed traversals). A “closeout” produces an **exit edge** (e_{\text{exit}}\in E) (or an exit-labeled edge in an augmented edge set).

Each place (p\in P) may have a capacity (\mathrm{cap}(p)\in\mathbb{N}). A **slot** is an indexed unit ((p,i)) with (i\in{1,\dots,\mathrm{cap}(p)}). Let custody be a set (U_q\subseteq {(p,i)}) at quantum (q).

A **quantized operational state** at quantum (q) can be modeled as
[
s_q = \big(p_q,\ o_q,\ U_q,\ b_q,\ h_q\big),
]
where:

* (p_q\in P) is the current place,
* (o_q\in\mathcal{O}) is the overlay posture (risk/privacy/constraint regime),
* (U_q) is slot custody,
* (b_q\in\mathbb{R}_{\ge 0}) is the visibility-ledger balance (in “minutes” units),
* (h_q) is the head pointer of the link-prev chain (hash / id of last accepted stamp).

A **stamp** (the atomic public/semipublic record unit) is a tuple
[
x_q = \big(\mathrm{id}_q,\ q,\ e_q,\ \mathrm{prev}_q,\ \nu_q,\ \mathrm{snap}_q,\ \tau_q,\ \Phi_q\big),
]
where:

* (\mathrm{id}_q) is a deterministic idempotent identifier,
* (e_q\in E) (or augmented edge labels) is the chosen edge/action,
* (\mathrm{prev}_q) is **link-prev** (a pointer/hash to prior state, typically (\mathrm{prev}*q = H(x*{q^-}))),
* (\nu_q) is an **edge-nonce** (fresh randomness to reduce correlation),
* (\mathrm{snap}_q) is a **snapshot-id** binding the stamp to a deterministic replay state,
* (\tau_q) is TTL (time-to-live) for the stamp and/or associated artifacts,
* (\Phi_q) is the minimized public field set (the “fingerprint surface”).

**Overlay-modulated TTL selection** can be captured by
[
\tau_q ;=; \mathrm{clip}\Big(m(o_q)\cdot \tau_0,\ \tau_{\min}(o_q),\ \tau_{\max}(o_q)\Big),
]
where (m(o)) is an overlay multiplier and (\mathrm{clip}(x,a,b)=\min(\max(x,a),b)).

**Ledger dynamics**: let (s_q\ge 0) be announce-spend posted (or accrued) at quantum (q), and (c_q\ge 0) be exit-comp-minutes credited at closeout/settlement. Then
[
b_{q+1} ;=; b_q + c_q - s_q,
\qquad\text{with invariant}\qquad b_q\ge 0\ \ \forall q.
]
A “net-zero check” is a post-closeout condition like (b_{q_\text{close}} \in [0,\varepsilon_b]).

**Edge ordering / custody safety** (capacity-limited places): if a place requires slot release before exit is considered valid, enforce an order constraint:
[
\text{(slot-release)} \prec \text{(exit-edge stamp)} \prec \text{(next-trigger stamp)},
]
both in chain order and in admissible timestamp order (after quantization). Correct closeout is the conjunction of (i) chain correctness, (ii) custody correctness, (iii) ledger non-negativity, and (iv) minimized (\Phi_q) under the active overlay.

