### Time quantization, pivots, and epsilon

**nearest-legal-quantum**: The closest admissible quantized timestamp that satisfies the rules for stamping (may depend on overlay posture, corridor legality, or system clock discipline). Used in restamp-after-rejection and time-quantum coalescing.

**epsilon**: A small tolerance parameter used to decide whether an exit vs placement pivot is “close enough” in time/space/quantum to coalesce, and to manage rounding/carry in settlement.
