### Announcements, minutes, settlement, and retention

**announce-events**: Public or semi-public events that disclose a bounded fact of activity (presence, spend, compliance) under a minimized field set. They’re inputs to settlement reconciliation.

**announce-spend**: The derived “cost” (in visibility units/minutes) computed from announce-events; aggregated for ledger updates and net-zero checks.

**comp-minutes**: The compensatory credit units minted/posted as part of settlement, typically reflecting compliant closeout behavior or matched announce spend.

**exit-comp-minutes**: The specific comp-minutes posted at exit time (or immediately after) and tied to the exit-edge stamp; it is the ledger-side counterpart to an exit.

**visibility-ledger**: The accounting system tracking spend (announce-spend) and credits (comp-minutes), enforcing non-negativity and reconciliation between announce events and exit credits.
